WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
now  the polish prime minister matteis  morovietsky has called the labor crisis  excuse me the border crisis with belarus  the greatest attempt to destabilize  europe since the cold war the  humanitarian situation shows no signs of  easing as poland continues to push back  migrants trying to cross illegally they  face harsh winter conditions out in the  forest along the border another migrant  has been buried by members of poland's  muslim community more than 10 people  have died in recent weeks while trying  to cross into the european union  and for more we're joined now by our  reporter amy and isif who is in the  polish city of ha nyovka  amien i know you've been out there for a  few days now just tell us about what the  situation is there today  as you said christine the situation  shows no sign of abating the checkpoints  here like the one you see behind me are  still firmly in place all throughout the  region near the border  the exclusion zone around the border is  also still firmly in place  keeping anybody from the media or from  aid organizations from accessing the  area around the border about 6 000  troops have been deployed here and more  are coming estonia has promised 100  troops um the uk has uh promised a  hundred as well as you can see there's a  military vehicle passing me right now a  lot of military activity in the region  that's because the polish border guard  says that every night around 200 people  tried to breach the border into poland  from the belarusian side we know for a  fact that several people had made it  through last night we had contact  through a source  that showed us dropped us a pin where  these people were camped out on the  polish side and that is worrying because  these temperatures have been dropping  this is the coldest day so far this week  around -3 celsius or 25 degrees  fahrenheit last night and hypothermia is  the number one reason why people get  sent by migrants have been sent to  hospitals in poland according to local  volunteers  um we know that hundreds of migrants are  still stranded in the forest we also  know that others were taken into  shelters in belarus can you give us an  overview of that situation  it's very difficult christine to give  any kind of overview of a situation like  this because of the media blackout in  this area in the woods around the border  as i said we had contact through a  source of people who were in the woods  but contact with the people themselves  is very difficult the number one reason  being that they're hiding from  authorities they don't trust many people  to to contact them  because they know that if they are found  either by emergency services or by the  police they will they there's a chance  that they will be brought immediately  back to the fence and illegally pushed  back to belarus poland has a law in  place  since the end of october that says they  can do this even though it's illegal  according to international law so what  is really happening to the migrants is a  mystery but what we do see is when they  do come out of the woods when they're  desperate enough to call the the medical  services and risk being sent back to  belarus they end up in a hospital or  they end up as you said uh being buried  because they did not survive the cold  nights here in the woods without a tent  or any resources  amy how is the polish government  handling this crisis and what support  is poland getting from the european  union  the polish government has more or less  split this into two different issues the  humanitarian issue which they put over  to the belarusian side and the political  issue now they've really only taken up  the mantle of the political issue that's  why uh the prime minister has been doing  a tour of the baltic states to drum up  support for the polish military the  polish border guard but they haven't  been addressing the humanitarian issue  now on the political side of course  there is no signs of de-escalation the  the polish side is in fact escalating by  bringing in more troops trying to  show a display of force against belarus  they've warned of  more things to come they said more  worrying things to come meaning that  this could devolve into a real conflict  with belarus but the humanitarian side  as i said has not been addressed that  crisis is ongoing we've seen  the the council of europe call for  poland to allow aid workers to get into  this  region of woods just beyond where i'm  standing where uh for now they have no  access and as i said winter is coming  this is going to devolve into a worse  situation if nothing is done about that  all right that's dwe's reporter amy and  um in the polish town of hanyovka that's  at that border between poland and  belarus thank you amy and for your  reporting

